      "artist": "Beyond My Ken",
      "credit": "Own work",
      "source": "2019 Seeley Stable Museum 1",
      "description": "The Seeley Stable Museum of the Old Town San Diego State Historic Park was built c.1869 by Albert Seeley, who ran a stage line between San Diego and Los Angeles.  He enlarged the stable with a single-story addition in the rear, new sheds, fencing, and a windmill used to pump water.  The bard was demolished in the late 1920s and reconstructed in 1975.  It is now a museum of 19th-century overland transportation gear and vehicles donated by Roscoe E. Hazard. (Source: The Seeley Stable)",
